      "side": 1,
      "message": "I racked my brain a lot over this.  LMK what you think if this pattern that I use (in one form or another) in 3 places to avoid the conditional \"don\u0027t forget to put it back\" code.\n\n```\n        let (new_state, reservation) \u003d match desc.state.take() {\n            Some(DescriptorState::Reserved(reservation)) \u003d\u003e (None, Ok(reservation)),\n            None \u003d\u003e {\n                pr_warn!(\n                    \"EINVAL from range_alloc.reservation_abort - offset: {}\",\n                    offset\n                );\n                (None, Err(EINVAL))\n            }\n            allocated \u003d\u003e {\n                pr_warn!(\n                    \"EPERM from range_alloc.reservation_abort - offset: {}\",\n                    offset\n                );\n                (allocated, Err(EPERM))\n            }\n        };\n\n        desc.state \u003d new_state;\n        let reservation \u003d reservation?;\n```",
